    logP = 2.4);
  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Lorazepam is a benzodiazepine used for anxiety and anxiety disorders, insomnia, status epilepticus and other epileptic seizures, catatonia, vomiting, and related sleep-wake and neurotic disorders. It is an approved medicine and appears on the WHO list of essential medicines, so it is widely used, though it carries a boxed warning.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q408265\">Wikidata Q408265</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>lorazepam</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>N05BA06</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=\"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB00186\">DB00186</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=\"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/3958\">3958</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:6539\">6539</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q408265\">Q408265</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C15H10Cl2N2O2</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>321.157 g/mol (PubChem CID 3958)</td></tr><tr><td>logP:</td><td>2.4 (Drugs.Common 25.09, not verified)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
